          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "To install an older version of ChatGPT-like Python packages on Termux (Android), follow these steps:  \n\n### **Step 1: Install Termux**  \nIf you haven’t already, install **Termux** from F-Droid (recommended) or another trusted source.  \n\n### **Step 2: Update Termux & Install Python**  \nOpen Termux and run:  \n```sh\npkg update && pkg upgrade -y\npkg install python -y\n```\n\n### **Step 3: Install a Specific Version of OpenAI’s `chatgpt` or `openai` Package**  \nIf you want an older version of OpenAI’s library for ChatGPT, use:  \n```sh\npip install openai==0.x.y  # Replace with the specific version\n```\nFor example:  \n```sh\npip install openai==0.27.2\n```\n\nIf you want to install an older chatbot package like `chatterbot`:  \n```sh\npip install chatterbot==1.0.5\n```\n\n### **Step 4: Verify Installation**  \nRun:  \n```sh\npython -m pip show openai\n```\nor  \n```sh\npython -m pip show chatterbot\n```\nThis will display the installed version.  \n\n### **Step 5: Test a Basic Chatbot**  \nCreate a Python script (`chatbot.py`):  \n```python\nimport openai\n\nopenai.api_key = \"your_api_key_here\"  # Replace with an actual API key\n\nresponse = openai.ChatCompletion.create(\n    model=\"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello, how are you?\"}]\n)\n\nprint(response[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"])\n```\nRun it:  \n```sh\npython chatbot.py\n```\n\nLet me know if you need help with a specific package!"
          ]
        },
