        "create_time": 1739463911.442254,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "To install an **older version of Python** in **Termux**, follow these steps:  \n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Uninstall Current Python Version (If Installed)**  \nFirst, remove any existing Python installation:  \n```sh\npkg uninstall python -y\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Use PRoot (If Needed)**  \nSince Termux only provides the latest Python version via `pkg`, you may need **PRoot** to run an older version. Install it:  \n```sh\npkg install proot proot-distro -y\n```\nThen, choose a lightweight Linux distribution like Debian:  \n```sh\nproot-distro install debian\nproot-distro login debian\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Install a Specific Older Version of Python**  \nNow, inside the PRoot (Debian environment), check available Python versions:  \n```sh\napt-cache show python3 | grep Version\n```\nTo install an older version (e.g., **Python 3.8**):  \n```sh\napt install python3=3.8*\n```\n\nIf the above command doesn’t work, try downloading a specific version:  \n```sh\napt install wget -y\nwget https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.8.10/Python-3.8.10.tar.xz\ntar -xf Python-3.8.10.tar.xz\ncd Python-3.8.10\n./configure && make && make install\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4: Verify Installation**  \nCheck the installed Python version:  \n```sh\npython3 --version\n```\n\nLet me know if you need help with a specific version!"
          ]
        },
