    "51d8d670-e594-471f-a452-d0ac4c082b12": {
      "id": "51d8d670-e594-471f-a452-d0ac4c082b12",
      "message": {
        "id": "51d8d670-e594-471f-a452-d0ac4c082b12",
        "author": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "name": null,
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "create_time": 1739464029.970405,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "PyTorch does **not officially support Termux** due to missing dependencies, but you can install it with a workaround.  \n\n### **Compatible Python Versions for PyTorch on Termux**  \n- **Python 3.8 - 3.10** is the safest range.  \n- **Python 3.11+** may cause compatibility issues.  \n\n### **How to Install PyTorch on Termux**  \n\n#### **Step 1: Install Python & Required Packages**  \n```sh\npkg update && pkg upgrade -y\npkg install python=3.10 clang cmake libjpeg-turbo ffmpeg git -y\npip install --upgrade pip\n```\n\n#### **Step 2: Install PyTorch via Pip (Try an Older Version if Needed)**  \n```sh\npip install torch torchvision torchaudio\n```\nIf the latest version fails, try an older one (e.g., 1.12.1):  \n```sh\npip install torch==1.12.1 torchvision==0.13.1 torchaudio==0.12.1\n```\n\n#### **Step 3: Verify Installation**  \nRun:  \n```sh\npython -c \"import torch; print(torch.__version__)\"\n```\n\nIf you get errors related to missing libraries, you may need to **compile PyTorch manually**, which is complex on Termux. Let me know if you need guidance on that!"
          ]
        },
