        "create_time": 1739464091.086733,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "### **Installing Python 3.10 on Termux**  \n\nBy default, Termux provides the latest Python version via `pkg`, but if you need **Python 3.10**, you can install it using a workaround.\n\n---\n\n### **Method 1: Using PRoot (Recommended)**\nSince Termux doesn't support installing older Python versions directly, you can use **PRoot with Debian/Ubuntu**.\n\n#### **Step 1: Install PRoot and Debian**\n```sh\npkg update && pkg upgrade -y\npkg install proot proot-distro -y\nproot-distro install debian\nproot-distro login debian\n```\n\n#### **Step 2: Install Python 3.10 in Debian**\nInside the Debian PRoot shell, run:\n```sh\napt update && apt upgrade -y\napt install software-properties-common -y\nadd-apt-repository ppa:deadsnakes/ppa -y\napt update\napt install python3.10 python3.10-venv python3.10-dev -y\n```\n\n#### **Step 3: Verify Installation**\n```sh\npython3.10 --version\n```\nYou should see output like:  \n```\nPython 3.10.x\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Method 2: Compile Python 3.10 from Source (Advanced & Slow)**\nIf you **don’t want to use PRoot**, you can **compile Python 3.10 manually** in Termux:\n\n#### **Step 1: Install Dependencies**\n```sh\npkg update && pkg upgrade -y\npkg install clang make tar xz-utils openssl libffi zlib -y\n```\n\n#### **Step 2: Download and Compile Python 3.10**\n```sh\nwget https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.10.12/Python-3.10.12.tar.xz\ntar -xf Python-3.10.12.tar.xz\ncd Python-3.10.12\n./configure --prefix=$HOME/.local\nmake -j$(nproc)\nmake install\n```\n\n#### **Step 3: Add Python 3.10 to PATH**\n```sh\necho 'export PATH=$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH' >> ~/.bashrc\nsource ~/.bashrc\n```\n\n#### **Step 4: Verify**\n```sh\npython3.10 --version\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Final Notes**\n- **Method 1 (PRoot)** is easier and safer.\n- **Method 2 (Compiling)** takes **30-60 minutes** depending on your device.\n- If you just need Python 3.10 **for a specific project**, using a **virtual environment** inside PRoot is the best approach.\n\nLet me know if you need help with any step!"
          ]
        },
